### Create router with createBrowserRouter and render with RouterProvider

Source: https://reactrouter.com/start/data/installation

Creates a browser router outside the React component tree and renders it using RouterProvider. Data Routers should not be held in React state.

```tsx
import React from "react";
import ReactDOM from "react-dom/client";
import { createBrowserRouter } from "react-router";
import { RouterProvider } from "react-router/dom";

const router = createBrowserRouter([
  {
    path: "/",
    element: <div>Hello World</div>,
  },
]);

const root = document.getElementById("root");

ReactDOM.createRoot(root).render(
  <RouterProvider router={router} />,
);
```
